**Placeholders:** `R=~/work/ccs.ansible`; `O` is my scratch root (backlog, `quorum/`, `inbox/`); `<…>` is a value read from the previous output. This session is set to English, so the operator texts are in English, although the manifest's §15 names Russian.

## 1. Read state — Bash, foreground, read-only

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || exit 1
herdr agent list
herdr agent read adv-codex --source visible --lines 5
herdr agent read adv-fable --source visible --lines 5
git -C $R fetch origin && git -C $R rev-parse origin/main
git -C $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain
ps -ax -o pid,command | grep -i '[c]odex'
codex plugin list </dev/null | grep -i superpowers
pmset -g assertions | grep -E 'PreventUserIdleSystemSleep|PreventSystemSleep'
```

## 2. Backlog — Edit, then Bash foreground, then Artifact

- WG relay row: status `docs closed`, `docs closed: no: snapshot, spec/plan status, memory`, next step "docs → cleanup".
- New row "RDP audio": status `brainstorm`, owners `prod-codex`/`prod-fable`, decisions: the operator's words, 2026-09-28.

Then `bash $O/orchestrator/build-backlog.sh` and republish the same Artifact page.

## 3. Close the relay's docs — prose subagent, background

```bash
# foreground
git -C $R worktree add $R/.claude/worktrees/wgka-docs -b chore/soul-ccs-it-wg-keepalive origin/main
```

I write `$O/wgka/evidence-canary.md` from my own logs: the deploy recap, the read-only verification, the re-run `changed=0`, the operator's ping summary and "accepted", PR #165 and its merge SHA.

Agent tool, `model: sonnet`, background:

> Reply in English. DIR: `<abs>/.claude/worktrees/wgka-docs` (base origin/main @ `<sha>`). Edit only inside DIR; do not commit, push or touch any host.
> EVIDENCE: `<O>/wgka/evidence-canary.md` is the only source of live facts; mark anything it does not show "not verified".
> 1. `projects/ccs/soul/ccs-it.md`: bring the gateway section to the state the evidence shows.
> 2. `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-27-ccs-wg-keepalive-relay-design.md` and `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-28-ccs-wg-keepalive-relay.md`: status line "implemented, PR #165, `<merge sha>`, canary ccs-it accepted 2026-09-28".
> 3. Do not edit `CLAUDE.md`, `KVM.md` or `docs/orchestration.md`; list every passage the relay makes stale.
> 4. Write the PR body to `<O>/wgka/pr-body.md`.
>
> No session links, no secrets, no change to any key, value, template or test. REPORT: `git diff --stat`, each claim with its evidence line, the list from item 3.

## 4. Stage 0 for RDP audio — two product advisors

```bash
# foreground
mkdir -p $O/brainstorm/rdp-audio
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $O/brainstorm/rdp-audio --label prod-codex --env ORCH_INBOX=$O/inbox --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $O/brainstorm/rdp-audio --label prod-fable --env ORCH_INBOX=$O/inbox --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```

Brief file `brief-r1-codex.txt`; the fable copy differs only in "advisor B" and `draft-fable.md`:

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the main
tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI suggestion,
never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.
TASK       T<n> — RDP audio
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file exists and you have reported its path
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go."
FACTS      CLAUDE.md, In-VM stack item 10 (rdp_server): one libvnc bridge to Xvnc:1, no
           xorgxrdp, "audio out of scope (phase 2)"; Gateway VM (v4): stream.d/rdp.conf.
           docs/v3/30-rdp.md; docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-21-ccs-rdp-lan-ccs-password-design.md.
           Nothing about audio has been measured on a host: ask me for host facts.
DECIDED    CLAUDE.md hard rules 1-18 bind, notably #1, #2, #7, #9, #14, #17. The deadline in
           the operator's words shortens no step of the skill.
MAY        read ~/work/ccs.ansible (origin/main @ <sha>), upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <O>/brainstorm/rdp-audio/draft-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact the
           other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal (question +
           2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and draft nothing
           that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   60 min for this round; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

```bash
# Bash, run_in_background: true — one call per tab
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $O/brainstorm/rdp-audio/brief-r1-codex.txt)" --wait --timeout 3600000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $O/inbox/prod-codex.last
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat $O/brainstorm/rdp-audio/brief-r1-fable.txt)" --wait --timeout 3600000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $O/inbox/prod-fable.last
```

- **If the Codex skill check in step 1 comes back empty:** I do not dispatch to `prod-codex`; I poll the operator to install it.
- **Later rounds:** round 2 swaps the draft paths and round 3 merges. Every open question goes to both voters at once as a neutral ballot.
- **Gate:** the confirmed joint doc goes to the 2/2 vote, then as an Artifact with a sign-off poll to the operator (hard rule #9). No executor exists before that.

## 5. Voting advisors — background, only for a tab at 50% or more

```bash
herdr agent prompt adv-fable "/compact mid-task: keep the protocol, the decisions with ballot ids and the open items" --wait --timeout 300000
herdr agent prompt adv-codex "/compact" --wait --timeout 300000
```

Each is followed by a request for a one-line status.

## 6. Poll — AskUserQuestion, only if step 1 shows nothing keeps the Mac awake

"The design runs overnight in agent tabs on your workstation; a sleeping Mac cuts their turns. Keep it awake until morning?"

1. Yes, run `caffeinate -is -t 36000` (recommended).
2. No, the work pauses when the Mac sleeps.
3. I will set it myself.

## 7. Status to the operator

> **Now.** The WireGuard keepalive relay (the small gateway server that passes the VPN client's keepalive, so tunnels stop rebuilding) is accepted on ccs-it and is being closed tonight: live-state snapshot, spec and plan status, memory note, then cleanup. "RDP audio" is in the backlog as a new task; two design advisors are writing independent drafts, round 1 of 3.
> **Next.** Cross-critique, one joint design, a vote by the two voting advisors, then the design as an Artifact with a sign-off poll for you. No code before that.
> **By morning.** The full process runs overnight and no step is shortened. An advisor split, or a fact only you hold, waits for you as a poll. If the full brainstorm cannot finish by morning, you get a poll: slip the deadline or waive the brainstorm.
> **You.** Nothing.
> **Vote decisions since the last status.** None.
> **Verified.** Deploy from merged main (PR #165); my re-run `changed=0`; your ping, 0% loss over 3 minutes. **Not verified:** anything beyond that window; nothing about audio on any host.
> **Live changes.** None since your acceptance; ccs-ops untouched.
> **Backlog.** `<link>`

## 8. On the subagent's notification

I check every claim against the evidence, then:

```bash
# foreground, in the docs worktree
git diff --stat origin/main                      # *.md only
git grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"          # must be empty
git add -A && git commit -m "docs(soul): ccs-it gateway with the WireGuard keepalive relay" -m "Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
git push -u origin chore/soul-ccs-it-wg-keepalive
gh pr create --title "docs(soul): ccs-it gateway with the WireGuard keepalive relay" --body-file $O/wgka/pr-body.md
gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch
```

Then I write memory note `ccs-wg-keepalive-relay.md` (type `project`) and its `MEMORY.md` line: canary accepted 2026-09-28, the loopback console port as the cause, rollback restores the failure, ccs-ops has no relay.

```bash
# foreground; worktrees removed only if status --porcelain is empty
herdr agent get wgka                             # focused must be false
herdr tab close <tab_id>
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wgka-docs
git -C $R worktree prune
git -C $R branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/soul-ccs-it-wg-keepalive
kill 48211                                       # after ps confirms it is my codex app-server
git -C $R pull && git -C $R worktree list
```

Backlog: `docs closed: yes`, `done`; republish.

## Why

- **Accepted is not done.** `done` needs the docs closed and the cleanup finished. "Harmless" and "paperwork any time" are how `soul/ccs-it.md` stays wrong for the next session. The close-out runs in the background of the new task and delays nothing.
- **"Go" starts the task, not an executor.** RDP audio is new user-visible behaviour, so it enters at stage 0: two product advisors, the 2/2 vote, then the operator's sign-off under hard rule #9. I hand over facts with paths and design nothing.
- **`wgka` is not reused.** One tab is one task, and it is an executor; design here is not an executor's job. What it knows is in the repository, which the product advisors read.
- **"By morning" is a wish.** It waives no gate. A night is enough for three rounds if nothing splits, so there is no conflict to poll yet.
- **The sleep poll** is the only question, because the workstation is the operator's and a sleeping Mac is the real threat to an overnight run.
- **Nine hours in,** the backlog, the ballot files and memory hold the state, not my context.
